      "c-88c922672add5cba": {
        "fuente": {
          "entradaId": "freeman-448",
          "modulo": "freeman-manners-customs"
        },
        "texto": "There is thought to be an allusion here to a custom which was practiced in Egypt in connection with the worship of the sacred calf, Apis. Godwyn says: “The party that repaired unto him tendered a bottle of hay or grass; which, if he received, then it betokened a good and happy ev…",
